<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gerardo Barrios</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1813–1865</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gerardo Barrios was a Salvadoran general and liberal president from 1859 to 1863, a follower of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-morazan">Francisco Morazán</a>'s dream of Central American union. He promoted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> cultivation, education and a professional army, and clashed with the Church. Overthrown in 1863 by the Guatemalan forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rafael-carrera">Rafael Carrera</a>, he was captured after a failed attempt to return and executed in 1865.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gerardo-barrios.jpg" alt="Gerardo Barrios" width="300" height="373" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Italo Lopez Vallecillos · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gerardo_Barrios.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
